      {
        "section_id": "nav:jamieson-fausset-brown:PSA.73:P:psa-73-1-28-of-asaph-see-introduction-god-is-good-to-his-people-for-although-t",
        "navigation_id": "PSA.73:P:psa-73-1-28-of-asaph-see-introduction-god-is-good-to-his-people-for-although-t",
        "scope": "passage",
        "role": "passage_overview",
        "title": "Psa 73:1-28 . Of Asaph--(see Introduction). God is good to His people. For although the prosperity of the wicked, and the afflictions of the righteous, tempted the Psalmist to misgivings of God's government, yet the sudden and fearful ruin of the ungodly, seen in the light of God's revelation, reassures his heart; and, chiding himself for his folly, he is led to confide renewedly in God, and celebrate His goodness and love."
      }
